t at the $2.5%$ significance level.\n\nThe teachers sampled $48$ students from School X and $55$ students from School Y and found that the first sample has a mean score of $82$ points and a standard deviation of $5$ points, while the second sample has a mean score of $75$ points and a standard deviation of $4$ points.\n\nAssuming that the population variances are the same for both samples, which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The $2.5%$ **one-tailed** critical region for the test statistic is approximately $T \\ge 1.984$\n2. At the $2.5%$ level of significance, there is **insufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} > μ_{y}$\n3. At the $2.5%$ level of significance, there is **sufficient** evidence that $μ_{x} > μ_{y}$\n\n*Hint: Given a random variable $T$ that has a student's $t$-distribution $T_{k}$ with $k$ degrees of freedom, the table below shows the $t$-scores $t_{k, p}$ such that $P(T > t_{k, p}) = p$ for some particular values of $k$ and $p$.*\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.100$ | $0.050$ | $0.025$ | $0.010$ | $0.005$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $100$ | $1.290$ | $1.660$ | $1.984$ | $2.364$ | $2.626$ |\n| $101$ | $1.290$ | $1.660$ | $1.984$ | $2.364$ | $2.625$ |\n| $102$ | $1.290$ | $1.660$ | $1.983$ | $2.363$ | $2.625$ |\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172113 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8dbf652d-3a37-51a3-bcd7-6d02ef98c033" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Sine Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050172 :topic/math-academy-id 3540 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Sine Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "997848ad-a62e-566f-9a17-c61a003df12e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186170908} {:answer/id #uuid 