ifficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "098d9a26-30b9-593f-93e1-d543e66fd2ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-95703" :question/problem "Which of the following equations define a non-empty set of points in the ${x}_{1}{x}_{2}$-plane?\n\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}=6$\n- ${x}_{1}^{2}+\\frac{{x}_{2}^{2}}{5}=-1$\n- ${x}_{2}^{2}=-7$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}=6$ defines a non-empty set. It represents two parallel lines, ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{6}$ and ${x}_{1}=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+\\frac{{x}_{2}^{2}}{5}=-1$ defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-negative for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ while the right-hand side is negative.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{2}^{2}=-7$ defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-negative for all ${x}_{2},$ while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172626 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050312 :topic/math-academy-id 3334 :topic/title "Sets and Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3f47263-f648-53f4-a10c-38be6c164957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171382} {:answer/id #uuid "00f0c90c-d225-5534-923f-b4aa0053151a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171383} {:answer/id #uuid "3c7fa33d-4e33-51fc-9184-22250deb22f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186171384} {:answer/id #uuid "41f23029-61db-5206-b