-22cd37903dc1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174172}] :question/id #uuid "c135d2ab-fff6-55ac-8ed4-c68105b83243" :question/math-academy-id "q-133924" :question/problem "There is a correlation between \"the temperature outside is hot\" and \"people buy more ice cream.\" Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. An increase in temperature causes people to buy more ice cream.\n2. An increase in ice cream sales causes an increase in temperature.\n3. More people outside causes the temperature to rise and people to buy more ice cream."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176026 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d95d1fdb-741d-5856-8a56-951412cf3575" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Causation vs. Coincidence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049775 :topic/math-academy-id 3589 :topic/title "Correlation vs. Causation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82eb1a4e-ce09-506d-a653-3ac87f6e5572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174179} {:answer/id #uuid "8ea77587-5f74-584e-8789-113577500378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174180} {:answer/id #uuid "053e0e7b-0d5b-5c20-bff2-ee5d7e7ace37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174181} {:answer/id #uuid "79e4e273-c333-5775-ac3c-0515886dc65b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174182} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecbae5e-724f-569e-b770-910a5d048081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174183}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d07e844a-3392-5054-9e6c-b45c1a2863b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174178}] :question/id #uuid "aa8bff27-5c5b-5841-8207-48990d736229" :question/math-academy-id "q-133925" :question/problem "Sally, an athlete, records everything she eats and drinks. She found a correlation between her drinking more water and a higher calorie intake. Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. Drinking more water causes Sally to consume more calories.\n2. Consuming more calories causes Sally to drink more water.\n3. The correlation between drinking more water and a higher calorie intake is coincidental."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176026 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d95d1fdb-741d-5856-8a56-951412cf3575" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Causation vs. Coincidence" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049775 :topic/math-academy-id 3589 :topic/title "Correlation vs. Causation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "843b5aed-0e47-5b07-8ea3-ee0cf5f8041f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174185} {:answer/id #uuid "f77d3ba9-8173-52da-806a-551f8de1fb38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174186} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b2942-c7bf-528a-a963-96ae166ef10f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174187} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1552be-7976-5b3f-87a6-4b422484b8e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174188} {:answer/id #uuid "66a1ba25-146c-5b3a-9d8b-563aee277542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174189}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c7b34320-9fcb-5b1a-abee-14584327ecb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174184}] :question/id #uuid "be62abc0-7f40-54ab-8dc1-c5e541301d69" :question/math-academy-id "q-133927" :question/problem "![](images/ea/ea92446f4d37e716886464b4e175aca26e796d67cdcb9f527d82afafb7817393.png)\n\nThe scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the number of dogs at particular kennels around the country and the amount of dog food consumed in a month (in kilograms). Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. An increase in the amount of dog food consumed causes an increase in the number of dogs.\n2. An increase in the number of dogs causes an increase in the amount of dog food consumed.\n3. The correlation between the number of dogs and the food consumed is coincidental."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176027 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dde7e70b-f4cb-508c-b402-b709bc68d676" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Causation vs. Multiple Causations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049775 :topic/math-academy-id 3589 :topic/title "Correlation vs. Causation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abef0e32-3b3a-5903-a952-22b4a841a2ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174191} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ae61fc-727a-5d68-aec1-fc6e667907ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174192} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b26690-1fdb-5ace-8952-c3cd7dff4f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174193} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec6b937-86dd-5495-9326-aef8108c8606" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174194} {:answer/id #uuid "68269fa3-27cb-5223-b913-94dd51073f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174195}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5017a2b4-a235-5621-8f64-098d54e4891f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174190}] :question/id #uuid "5d685893-0708-57fc-8faf-728c0d2fd5e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-133930" :question/problem "![](images/71/716be3363620a0be576096e37149ed310720a9be3794b5a9a850fe04bca5795a.png)\n\nJake is practicing his baseball batting. The scatter plot above shows the correspondence between the angle at which Jake hits the ball and the distance the ball travels (in feet). Which of the following is most likely true?\n\n1. An increase in the angle of contact is the only cause of an increase in the distance traveled.\n2. An increase in force the ball is struck is the only cause of an increase in the distance traveled.\n3. The angle of contact and the force the ball is struck are both factors that influence the distance traveled."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176025 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0539bb48-e4f7-505d-a40e-f03520615f7e" :knowledge-point/title "Causation vs. Outside Causations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049775 :topic/math-academy-id 3589 :topic/title "Correlation vs. Causation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85757bc0-e738-57d2-9af3-dad3f6946406" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174209} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fd76e2-d970-582c-976b-b78fb6a9f224" :answer/type {:db/id #