he function $y = \\cot x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has asymptotes at $x = nπ$.\n2. The function takes positive values on the intervals $(nπ, \\frac{π}{2} + nπ)$.\n3. The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x = nπ$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176055 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050427 :topic/math-academy-id 3566 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac0c42e3-1989-5d76-9af2-dcd67e9522ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174871} {:answer/id #uuid "c8aae479-4508-5983-ae47-f31adfdbe903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174872} {:answer/id #uuid "eb3828c5-066d-5b6a-901c-26819b0b8bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174873} {:answer/id #uuid "0aa324e2-4a15-5627-85ff-ccad8d10339a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174874} {:answer/id #uuid "5c3e0d14-2757-5efc-801f-b09a1b399cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174875}] :answer-field/id #uuid "612de9c0-4053-58d4-8209-eaa9d7f2a81a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174870}] :question/id #uuid "e47c0a25-f708-54a4-a2a5-325848a3aed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-27823" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\cot x$?\n\n1. The function has asymptotes at $x = ± \\frac{π}{2}, ± \\frac{3π}{2}, …$.\n2. The range of the function is $(-\\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2})$.\n3. The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$, where $n$ is an integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba9d2401-4e30-5327-b8eb-b4db7108dd0c" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Linear Transformations in the Cartesian Plane" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049895 :topic/math-academy-id 3645 :topic/title "The Image of a Linear Transformation in the Cartesian Plane"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d50a84ab-12b6-5677-9fb2-0cabf243c948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174995} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5c80aa-4a7f-5abc-a6d4-924798b9e894" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174996} {:answer/id #uuid "0683e590-fee2-5c5d-8c9f-ece0c141d390" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174997} {:answer/id #uuid "4c22144a-73e5-5d55-b565-268b0ecdad18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174998} {:answer/id #uuid "75339ba4-510b-5501-9cb7-5376775c78ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174999}] :answer-field/id #uuid "86694dcb-b693-5125-8719-fb13e5c0fbbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174994} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "205b2403-7246-564d-a8b4-99344c7bb198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366047} {:answer/id #uuid "0e2307a4-ae25-5241-b653-9087ca96fb95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366048} {:answer/id #uuid "c8b3fcbc-dc14-5e13-813e-4eec14ce7dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366049} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd3e109-9836-5ba4-9561-80af7ce47d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366050} {:answer/id #uuid "870436af-69e3-5c39-abfb-dfcb98e1601f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8b3fcbc-dc14-5e13-813e-4eec14ce7dea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366049} :answer-field/id #uuid "c38feedc-971f-5a1b-b15c-77787df222c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366046}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4acbb26f-7e4b-53ce-a37d-bd74763516c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38297" :question/problem "Consider a linear transformation $T$ that maps ${R}^{2}$ to the origin. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $\\text{rank}(T)=1$,  where $T$ is the standard matrix of $T$\n- $\\text{Im}(T)$ contains no vectors of ${R}^{2}$\n- $\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when the image of a linear transformation $T$ in ${R}^{2}$ with the standard matrix $T$ is the zero-subspace ${0},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=0\n$$\n\nand, according to the rank-nullity theorem, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{nullity}(T)=\\text{nullity}(T) & =2-\\text{rank}(T) \\\\  & =2-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In our case, we have \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The image of $T$ contains the vector zero vector $0=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, the condition $\\text{nullity}(T)=2$ in ${R}^{2}$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\n\\text{Ker}(T)={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176051 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0e2a8cf2-64db-5b2f-b0f7-0c727cf492a9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050359 :topic/math-academy-id 3563 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Secant Function"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ff17a58-8205-5149-bf09-c0063ddab754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175055} {:answer/id #uuid "a36d9b00-2b61-55ad-94ac-f79dccb8f586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175056} {:answer/id #uuid "c78155ea-682a-5623-ada9-451bb9431b48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "All" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175057} {:answer/id #uuid "0758280d-0aed-561c-8b42-424819a1b890" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175058} {:answer/id #uuid "4032b07b-9566-5037-9ada-0d471a8768d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175059}] :answer-field/